  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1209 PM MST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nThursday sees the long term period begin with continued calm and \ntranquil conditions, despite NM being saddled between an H5 low \ndigging way southward into western Mexico and another H5 low over \nthe TN/KY region. Light prevailing winds and highs persistent in the \n40s/50s remain the rule. \n\nFriday into the weekend sees strengthening northwesterly flow over \nthe state. Breezy to locally windy westerlies will be favored each \nafternoon over wind prone areas along the Continental Divide and \ncentral mountain chain. Downslope compressional warming lee of the \ncentral mountains will raise high temperatures considerably into the \n60s and even low 70s Saturday in southeastern NM as a result. \nNumerical models continue to advertise a shortwave trough of varying \nintensity clipping southeastern CO and northeastern NM. As such \nthere is a low chance for quick hitting precip. to reach the \nnorthern Sangre de Cristo's and adjacent Raton Pass area. Otherwise, \nthe main sensible weather impact will be a cold front backing \nsouthward through eastern NM bringing a drop in high temperatures \ninto the 50s again. \n\nWesterlies pickup in strength Monday as another shortwave trough \nclips northern NM, favoring light snow and precipitation over the \nnorthern mountains along the CO border. A more active weather \npattern is favored by the middle to latter portions of next week \nafter a quick ridge sliding over the area.",
